1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,500
Hey... tell me.

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:06,680
Tonight,

3
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,590
do you want to hold me?

4
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:26,580
I want to hold you.

5
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:32,820
Okay.

6
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,840
Hold me.

7
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
"The Servant Prince"
(Episode 5)

8
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,660
I used to think that being
held by you in a place like this

9
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,500
made me feel like an escort.

10
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:12,480
But it's actually not so bad.

11
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:21,890
Hey.

12
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,770
Next time you're in the mood,
you can just call me over.

13
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,230
I'll come here and let you hold me.

14
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,200
What's wrong?

15
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,580
Nothing.

16
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:50,620
Honestly, just hearing you say that
is enough to get me going ten times over.

17
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:52,460
Huh?

18
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,760
By the way,

19
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,940
why would you do it alone?

20
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:05,470
Didn't I tell you
that I want you to desire me too?

21
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,040
What a great reaction.

22
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,180
That tickles.

23
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,520
Hey, that tickles.

24
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:36,300
Get off me. You want to go again?

25
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,059
Huh? Wait, Takaaki?

26
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,060
Hey, hey.

27
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,379
Where do you think you're going?

28
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,860
Hey, Takaaki.

29
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,899
Wait, what are you doing?

30
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:49,900
Come on.

31
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,810
Hey, that's enough. I've had enough.

32
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:27,740
Huh.

33
00:04:28,510 --> 00:04:31,480
This is the first time
I've seen him sleeping.

34
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,160
Even though we've been
together for ten years.

35
00:04:38,610 --> 00:04:41,040
During those days of painful struggle,

36
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:43,950
Naoya.

37
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:46,700
Every time I woke up,

38
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,520
Takaaki.

39
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,280
Is it time?

40
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:58,270
Takaaki was always by my side,

41
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:02,550
naturally leaning in to check on me.

42
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:05,530
Ouch...

43
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,430
Are you okay?

44
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,520
Just how tense is this
guy when he's around me?

45
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:21,420
And what kind of feelings did
he have while watching over me?

46
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:28,050
He looks a bit younger
than when he's awake.

47
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:45,960
Thank you.

48
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,140
Naoya?

49
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,300
Good morning.

50
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:00,020
Takaaki, I'm hungry.

51
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,460
Also, lend me a change of clothes.

52
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:21,730
I can't believe I overslept.

53
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,420
For a second, I didn't
even know where I was.

54
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:28,856
If I knew you were coming, I
would've bought some groceries.

55
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,760
There's not much to eat
in the house right now.

56
00:06:32,510 --> 00:06:34,110
Anyway, I'll make you some coffee first.

57
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:35,970
Oh, sorry about that.

58
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:53,870
To think Naoya is actually here
in this dull, lifeless room.

59
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:59,070
The air here is slowly drawing
color from his presence.

60
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:05,840
Thanks.

61
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,840
Mhm.

62
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,300
It's good.

63
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,640
I'm glad.

64
00:07:17,030 --> 00:07:19,020
Drinking coffee this elegantly

65
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:21,690
is so out of character for my daily life.

66
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:29,500
Goto Construction just announced that a
customer data breach has been confirmed.

67
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:35,109
According to the statement, the email
addresses of about 53,000 customers

68
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:37,029
and their personal
information have been leaked.

69
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,250
Turn off the TV.

70
00:07:42,010 --> 00:07:43,680
I figured it was about time,

71
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,840
but this isn't exactly what you want
to hear first thing in the morning.

72
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:50,650
I remember Takaaki's company also...

73
00:07:51,459 --> 00:07:53,626
[Goto Construction]

74
00:07:53,930 --> 00:07:55,320
That company name...

75
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,740
Isn't that my dad's company?

76
00:07:58,390 --> 00:08:02,040
You guys were involved in
building their security system, right?

77
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,070
Did you do something?

78
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:10,530
I didn't do anything.

79
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:13,840
They canceled our contract a long time ago.

80
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:15,550
Huh?

81
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:20,870
It was about half a year ago.

82
00:08:22,370 --> 00:08:26,990
Goto Construction approached us, saying they
wanted to completely switch to our system.

83
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:31,230
But after looking into it, we found out

84
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:35,490
their old system was full of holes.

85
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:39,740
Even if we layered our
latest system on top of it,

86
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:43,620
there would still be a
risk of getting hacked.

87
00:08:48,350 --> 00:08:49,350
So you're saying,

88
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:55,670
the security of the system my dad's
company was using was just too weak?

89
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,240
Exactly.

90
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:01,850
Plus, the company that built the
old system had already dissolved,

91
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:04,540
leaving almost no documentation behind.

92
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:12,440
To fix it as quickly as possible, the terms
I proposed were all within necessary costs.

93
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,800
I see.

94
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:19,260
From our standpoint,
we couldn't make any more concessions.

95
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:22,140
You've got quite the nerve.

96
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,870
I heard you're also considering
partnering with other companies.

97
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:30,609
Word travels fast.

98
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:32,540
While it's highly regrettable,

99
00:09:32,564 --> 00:09:34,092
if you insist on forcing this
through with your original budget,

100
00:09:34,116 --> 00:09:35,765
then we have no choice
but to terminate our partnership.

101
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:37,479
Are you sure you want to say that?

102
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:40,380
You're just a newly established startup.

103
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:43,890
The one who rejected us
and went to another company

104
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,670
was that man.

105
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,310
That guy, seriously.

106
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,380
He actually skimped on
investing in a management system?

107
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:55,970
It was a complete misjudgment.

108
00:09:57,050 --> 00:09:59,300
So I knew this was going
to happen sooner or later.

109
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:02,760
As far as I'm concerned, he had it coming.

110
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:05,260
Let him squirm.

111
00:10:07,770 --> 00:10:08,770
Fair enough.

112
00:10:12,270 --> 00:10:14,150
I'm starving.

113
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:17,030
By the way,

114
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,110
do you not even have bread or rice here?

115
00:10:19,990 --> 00:10:20,990
Sorry.

116
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:23,950
Seriously,

117
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,640
you don't even really live here, do you?

118
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,520
You're hopeless.

119
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:34,270
Let's go buy something together.

120
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:36,170
Huh?
What?

121
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,340
Come on, let's go.

122
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:40,470
Ah...

123
00:10:59,070 --> 00:11:00,990
There are so few people
around at this hour.

124
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:05,050
There's a convenience store
just around that corner.

125
00:11:06,410 --> 00:11:07,660
That's really close.

126
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:09,710
Yeah.

127
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:11,390
Man,

128
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,880
I kind of wanted to walk a bit longer.

129
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,920
This makes us look like a couple, right?

130
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:50,810
Let's go.

131
00:12:15,290 --> 00:12:16,770
It's nice to do this once in a while.

132
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:18,290
Yeah.

133
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,450
Yeah.

134
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:30,000
Come to think of it,
we rarely eat breakfast together.

135
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,090
Whenever I woke up,

136
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:43,820
the breakfast Takaaki made for me
was always already sitting there.

137
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,600
Takaaki, you're still eating
salmon rice balls, huh.

138
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,830
And you've always stuck to tuna, Naoya.

139
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:00,270
Yeah.

140
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:02,630
Back in high school,

141
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:05,830
I used to treat you like an errand boy
and make you buy a bunch of stuff.

142
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:08,340
When they were sold out of tuna,

143
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:11,766
I'd rush all the way to a convenience store
in the next town over to get it.

144
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,790
Huh?

145
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:14,090
Did you really?

146
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:16,810
Naoya's orders were absolute.

147
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,840
I really was a jerk back then.

148
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:34,270
Takaaki.

149
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:37,900
I...

150
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,740
I'm actually planning
to get a full-time job.

151
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:42,960
Full-time?

152
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,320
Yeah.

153
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:48,950
The manager at my part-time job
asked if I wanted to go full-time.

154
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:54,120
I don't hate the work,

155
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:56,710
so I'm planning to give
her my answer today.

156
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:00,550
I see.

157
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:03,510
Is this because of that guy named Mori?

158
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:05,170
Huh?

159
00:14:05,590 --> 00:14:07,109
Are you scared or something?

160
00:14:07,110 --> 00:14:10,180
No, I just wanted to
know where your head's at.

161
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:12,970
Mori-san was just a catalyst.

162
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:16,810
I just want to stand
firmly on my own two feet.

163
00:14:18,130 --> 00:14:21,270
If I want freedom, I need to
build a solid foundation first.

164
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,070
A foundation, huh.

165
00:14:25,930 --> 00:14:27,030
Besides, Mori-san

166
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:28,960
is retiring this month.

167
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:32,370
Don't worry.

168
00:14:33,290 --> 00:14:35,580
You're all I have.

169
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:43,920
Yeah.

170
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:51,030
Ah, we both have to get to work, right?

171
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:52,290
Let's go.

172
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:56,560
Yeah.

173
00:14:56,870 --> 00:14:57,870
You're right.

174
00:15:12,090 --> 00:15:13,910
You're willing to go full-time?

175
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,040
That's great.

176
00:15:16,610 --> 00:15:17,699
Thank you.

177
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:18,700
No problem.

178
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:23,170
Now I can retire with peace of mind.

179
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:25,210
Though, with you here, Goto-kun,

180
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,380
I kind of want to come back to
work under the re-employment system.

181
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:30,130
Sure.

182
00:15:30,131 --> 00:15:31,451
We'll be waiting for you anytime.

183
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,390
Mori-san was just a catalyst.

184
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:51,030
I just want to stand
firmly on my own two feet.

185
00:15:52,190 --> 00:15:55,510
If I want freedom, I need to
build a solid foundation first.

186
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,260
Naoya is spreading his wings
and heading toward freedom.

187
00:16:00,870 --> 00:16:04,430
I really should be happy for
him from the bottom of my heart.

188
00:16:05,810 --> 00:16:06,810
But...

189
00:16:08,170 --> 00:16:10,880
I was the one who...

190
00:16:12,810 --> 00:16:15,010
That cramped little room in the past

191
00:16:16,310 --> 00:16:18,740
was Naoya's everything.

192
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:23,910
I can't help but miss it terribly.

193
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,120
Excuse me.

194
00:16:42,050 --> 00:16:45,830
President, Goto Construction is
asking about renewing the contract.

195
00:16:46,190 --> 00:16:46,920
I knew they'd come.
Yes.

196
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,646
They said they'd like to meet
with you as soon as possible.

197
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:52,989
And they've even offered
some very generous terms.

198
00:16:52,990 --> 00:16:53,840
How should we handle this?

199
00:16:53,841 --> 00:16:54,900
Reject them.

200
00:16:57,010 --> 00:16:58,429
Uh... but...

201
00:16:58,430 --> 00:16:59,870
Just do it. Turn them down.

202
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:03,990
Yes, sir.

203
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,730
I understand.

204
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:07,590
I'll get back to work.

205
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:19,590
Good work.

206
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:20,790
Good work.

207
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:27,080
Good work.

208
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:28,670
Heading home now?
Yeah.

209
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:31,510
Want to walk together for a bit?

210
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,320
Sure.

211
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:40,050
I'm so glad that you're becoming a
full-time employee, Goto-san.

212
00:17:40,450 --> 00:17:44,410
Not at all. I don't even know
if I can fill Mori-san's shoes.

213
00:17:44,590 --> 00:17:46,190
You don't need to fill anyone's shoes.

214
00:17:46,230 --> 00:17:48,610
As long as you bring your
own style to it, Goto-san,

215
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:52,280
this restaurant will definitely transform
and become even better.

216
00:17:53,910 --> 00:17:56,630
What are your plans
after retiring, Mori-san?

217
00:17:57,510 --> 00:18:01,300
I plan to travel the world.
It's always been a dream of mine.

218
00:18:02,090 --> 00:18:05,120
After all, this is the first time
I'll have so much free time.

219
00:18:06,370 --> 00:18:08,210
Free time, huh?

220
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:11,299
I was unemployed for two whole years,

221
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,589
and had all the free time in the world.

222
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:15,299
What was I even doing?

223
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:18,690
That just means that time
was necessary for you, too.

224
00:18:21,863 --> 00:18:22,863
I...

225
00:18:22,983 --> 00:18:27,040
I'll give it my all so that you won't be
disappointed when you visit again, Mori-san.

226
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,770
Then I'll have to buy extra souvenirs.

227
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:31,090
Huh?

228
00:18:31,091 --> 00:18:32,291
I'll be looking forward to it.

229
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:39,623
At the end of the month,
Mori-san retired as planned.

230
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,580
Thank you for waiting.

231
00:18:42,530 --> 00:18:45,530
And starting the following month, I
officially became a full-time employee.

232
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:50,630
Here is the pan-seared
sea bream with gravy.

233
00:18:50,910 --> 00:18:53,969
Excuse me, where is this sea bream from?

234
00:18:53,970 --> 00:18:55,650
It was caught in Hyogo Prefecture.

235
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:57,720
Goto-kun.

236
00:18:57,830 --> 00:19:00,220
He's doing great.

237
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:04,410
Lately, we've even had customers coming in
specifically to see Goto-san.

238
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:08,329
Looks like he's contributing
a lot to our sales.

239
00:19:08,330 --> 00:19:09,520
He really is.

240
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:14,570
It's so great that we could make
Goto-kun a full-time employee.

241
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,840
However, after becoming
a full-time employee,

242
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,670
unlike before, I'm tied up at
the restaurant for much longer.

243
00:19:22,070 --> 00:19:23,200
And I've gotten much busier.

244
00:19:25,130 --> 00:19:29,470
Which means my schedule
clashes with Takaaki's a lot more.

245
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,500
(I'm working until closing tonight,
so I'll be home late.)

246
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
(Okay.)

247
00:21:05,001 --> 00:21:09,800
(I went to your place but no one was there, so
I headed back. Call me when you get off work.)

248
00:21:10,290 --> 00:21:15,830
Did he really go back home
just to come over again when I got back?

249
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:57,520
Hey.

250
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:01,690
Whoa.

251
00:22:03,110 --> 00:22:06,200
You were taking too long to invite me over,
so I just came by myself.

252
00:22:07,010 --> 00:22:09,300
Even picked up some food on the way.

253
00:22:13,410 --> 00:22:14,410
Yeah.

254
00:22:16,790 --> 00:22:17,790
Hey...

255
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:21,310
You're about ready to hold me, aren't you?

256
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:44,420
Mind if I use the shower?

257
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:49,070
I haven't showered yet either.

258
00:22:53,090 --> 00:22:54,390
Let's shower together then.

259
00:22:57,030 --> 00:22:59,220
Shower play is an extra service, you know.

260
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:25,330
Wait, I'm gonna get dizzy.

261
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:28,400
Just get in.

262
00:24:30,630 --> 00:24:32,806
(Next Episode Preview)
Maybe I should just move in here.

263
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:35,510
If it's the UNI collaboration project,
please let me handle it.

264
00:24:35,590 --> 00:24:39,569
You can use this money to start a business,
or even buy a new apartment.

265
00:24:39,570 --> 00:24:40,830
I want to see you more.

